12d:T99d,![](/images/cms/64ca19af7fb75792749827-908a98.webp)

With Veridis' patented MADSCAN, discover the precise composition of your plastic streams and batches. Veridis offers the first batch-representative thermal analysis method for polymers, capable of distinguishing between different polymer types, subtypes, and their proportions within a batch.

As the demand for high-quality recycled plastic is expected to grow exponentially in the coming years, innovative and scalable new technologies for polymer analysis are essential to ensure quality and safety while meeting these increasing demands. With MADSCAN, Veridis enables highly accurate polymer insights on an industrial scale, right at the early stages of the recycling process.

![](/images/cms/64ca19af801f5005460366-3d4c4c.webp)

Here’s the translation into UK-Business-English:

\- Analyses both flakes and granulates, up to 1000 flakes/granulates per scan.

\- Detects various (sub)types of polyolefins, including PP, HDPE, LDPE, LLDPE, as well as PET in PO batches.

\- Accurately measures the size of each fraction in percentage (with a precision of 5%).

\- Analyses all colours, including carbon black and dark polymers.

\- Also analyses multilayer materials and films.

\- Capable of measuring washed flake input streams before extrusion or compounding.

Due to the larger volume that can be measured compared to existing (thermal) analysis methods, each scan with Veridis' MADSCAN can analyse up to 1000 flakes or granulates per scan, accurately measuring the proportions of HDPE, LDPE, LLDPE, PP, and PET within PE. This provides recyclers, processors, compounders, and brand owners using recyclates with precise and reliable polymer insights.

![](/images/cms/64ca19af806dd451478134-2f4134.webp)

## Technische Spezifikationen

| **INFO** | **SPECIFICATIONS** |
| --- | --- |
| Sample size | 50-500 grams |
| Measuring time | 1-2 hours |
| Temperature range | RT – 300°C |
| Sample types | Flakes, granulate and powder |
| Atmospheric conditions | N2 |
| Software | Peak separation, purity determination, determination of phase transitions (Tg, Tm, Tc), polymer identification and quantification. |
| Accuracy | ±1% ∆H |

**Here**you can download further MADSCAN product information and the roadmap.

A more advanced version of MADSCAN, the T-50 model, has also been recently released. You can find all the information about it [**here**](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-4ra87YVIWk).12e:"$EObject.defineProperty(function remarkGfm(options) {\n    // @ts-expect-error: TS is wrong about `this`.\n    // eslint-disable-next-line unicorn/no-this-assignment\n    const self = this;\n    const settings = options || emptyOptions;\n    const data = self.data();\n    const micromarkExtensions = data.micromarkExtensions || (data.micromarkExtensions = []);\n    const fromMarkdownExtensions = data.fromMarkdownExtensions || (data.fromMarkdownExtensions = []);\n    const toMarkdownExtensions = data.toMarkdownExtensions || (data.toMarkdownExtensions = []);\n    micromarkExtensions.push((0, __TURBOPACK__imported__module__$5b$project$5d2f$node_modules$2f$micromark$2d$extension$2d$gfm$2f$index$2e$js__$5b$app$2d$rsc$5d$__$28$ecmascript$29$__[\"gfm\"])(settings));\n    fromMarkdownExtensions.push((0, __TURBOPACK__imported__module__$5b$project$5d2f$node_modules$2f$mdast$2d$util$2d$gfm$2f$lib$2f$index$2e$js__$5b$app$2d$rsc$5d$__$28$ecmascript$29$__[\"gfmFromMarkdown\"])());\n    toMarkdownExtensions.push((0, __TURBOPACK__imported__module__$5b$project$5d2f$node_modules$2f$mdast$2d$util$2d$gfm$2f$lib$2f$index$2e$js__$5b$app$2d$rsc$5d$__$28$ecmascript$29$__[\"gfmToMarkdown\"])(settings));\n},\"name\",{value:\"remarkGfm\"})"
